WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.950
Oxford Bookworm's Library.

00:03.000 --> 00:04.950
Starter.

00:05.000 --> 00:07.950
The Girl with Green Eyes.

00:08.000 --> 00:09.950
By John Escott.

00:10.000 --> 00:13.950
Read by Christopher Ragland.

00:14.000 --> 00:20.000
Published and copyright, Oxford University Press 2012.

00:30.000 --> 00:37.950
The Girl with Green Eyes.

00:38.000 --> 00:44.950
Greg is a porter at the Shepton Hotel in New York.

00:45.000 --> 00:51.950
After work, he always goes for a coffee across the street.

00:52.000 --> 00:58.950
A girl is sitting in the coffee shop near the window.

00:59.000 --> 01:01.950
It's her again.

01:02.000 --> 01:03.950
Thanks Greg.

01:04.000 --> 01:07.950
She's here every afternoon.

01:08.000 --> 01:11.950
I'm going to say hello.

01:12.000 --> 01:18.950
Greg goes into the coffee shop and gets a coffee.

01:19.000 --> 01:24.000
Then he goes across to the girl's table.

01:25.000 --> 01:27.950
Hi, he says.

01:28.000 --> 01:29.950
I'm Greg.

01:30.000 --> 01:33.950
Can I sit with you?

01:34.000 --> 01:36.950
Okay, she says.

01:37.000 --> 01:40.950
I'm Cassie.

01:41.000 --> 01:47.950
I come here for a coffee every day after work, says Greg.

01:48.000 --> 01:52.950
I'm a porter at the Shepton Hotel.

01:53.000 --> 01:54.950
He smiles.

01:55.000 --> 01:59.950
You have beautiful green eyes.

02:00.000 --> 02:03.950
Have I? She says.

02:04.000 --> 02:07.950
She doesn't smile.

02:08.000 --> 02:12.950
Is something wrong, Cassie? He asks.

02:13.000 --> 02:17.950
You don't look very happy.

02:18.000 --> 02:23.950
It's nothing. She says.

02:24.000 --> 02:27.950
Tell me, says Greg.

02:28.000 --> 02:30.950
Maybe I can help.

02:31.000 --> 02:34.950
Well, she begins.

02:35.000 --> 02:39.950
Go on, says Greg.

02:40.000 --> 02:46.950
My stepfather is staying at the Shepton Hotel. She says.

02:47.000 --> 02:50.950
He has my sketchbooks.

02:51.000 --> 02:53.950
I'm an artist.

02:54.000 --> 02:59.950
When I ask him to give them to me, he says, no.

03:00.000 --> 03:04.950
I want you to come back home to Boston.

03:05.000 --> 03:09.950
But I don't want to go back to Boston.

03:10.000 --> 03:13.950
He's not nice.

03:14.000 --> 03:20.950
How long is he going to be at the hotel, asks Greg?

03:21.000 --> 03:25.950
Two more days, says Cassie.

03:26.000 --> 03:30.950
He's in room 724.

03:31.000 --> 03:36.950
Maybe I can get the sketchbooks for you, says Greg.

03:37.000 --> 03:41.950
Maybe I can get into his room.

03:42.000 --> 03:45.950
Can you? She says.

03:46.000 --> 03:53.950
Meet me here tomorrow afternoon at 4.30, says Greg.

03:54.000 --> 03:55.950
Okay.

03:56.000 --> 03:59.950
Thank you, says Cassie.

04:00.000 --> 04:02.950
Thank you very much.

04:03.000 --> 04:05.950
She looks at her watch.

04:06.000 --> 04:08.950
I've got to go now.

04:09.000 --> 04:12.950
See you tomorrow.

04:13.000 --> 04:21.950
When Cassie gets back to her hotel room, she makes a telephone call.

04:22.000 --> 04:25.950
Hello? She says.

04:26.000 --> 04:27.950
It's me.

04:28.000 --> 04:29.950
It's okay.

04:30.000 --> 04:32.950
The boy's going to do it.

04:33.000 --> 04:34.950
Yes.

04:35.000 --> 04:40.950
I'm going to get them from him tomorrow afternoon.

04:41.000 --> 04:42.950
Okay.

04:43.000 --> 04:48.950
I can meet you there the morning after at 10 a.m.

04:49.000 --> 04:51.950
Don't forget to bring the money.

04:52.000 --> 04:56.950
$2,000.

04:57.000 --> 05:02.950
Next morning, Greg arrives at work early.

05:03.000 --> 05:08.950
He goes to find room 724.

05:09.000 --> 05:16.950
I have to wait for Cassie's stepfather to go out, he thinks.

05:17.000 --> 05:24.950
I don't know his name, but it doesn't matter.

05:25.000 --> 05:31.950
Greg watches the door of room 724.

05:32.000 --> 05:38.950
He sees the girl come to clean the rooms.

05:39.000 --> 05:47.950
Some minutes later, a man comes out of room 724.

05:48.000 --> 05:54.950
That must be Cassie's stepfather, thinks Greg.

05:55.000 --> 06:06.950
He waits for the man to leave, and for the cleaning girl to go into room 724.

06:07.000 --> 06:12.950
I need to look in the room, he thinks.

06:13.000 --> 06:17.950
Greg waits for the girl to leave the bedroom.

06:18.000 --> 06:26.950
Then, he goes into the room and begins to look for the sketchbooks.

06:27.000 --> 06:30.950
I must be quick, he thinks.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.950
Where are they?

06:35.000 --> 06:41.950
Suddenly, Greg sees the sketchbooks by the bed.

06:42.000 --> 06:45.950
Got them, he thinks.

06:46.000 --> 06:50.950
He begins to look at the pictures.

06:51.000 --> 06:56.950
Wow, Cassie is a great artist.

06:57.000 --> 07:00.950
These are good.

07:01.000 --> 07:08.950
Greg is leaving the room when he hears the cleaning girl call out to him.

07:09.000 --> 07:11.950
Hey, she says.

07:12.000 --> 07:14.950
What are you doing?

07:15.000 --> 07:17.950
Come back.

07:18.000 --> 07:22.950
Greg does not stop.

07:23.000 --> 07:32.950
Greg finishes work that afternoon and leaves the hotel through a door in the next street.

07:33.000 --> 07:43.950
When he gets near the front of the hotel, he sees the man from room 724.

07:44.000 --> 07:47.950
That's him again, thinks Greg.

07:48.000 --> 07:52.950
That's Cassie's stepfather.

07:53.000 --> 07:57.950
Greg waits for the man to go into the hotel.

07:58.000 --> 08:03.950
Then, he goes to the coffee shop.

08:04.000 --> 08:09.950
Cassie is at the same table in the coffee shop.

08:10.000 --> 08:16.950
Greg gets a coffee and goes to sit with her.

08:17.000 --> 08:24.950
I have them, he says, and he puts the sketchbooks on the table.

08:25.000 --> 08:29.950
That's great, says Cassie.

08:30.000 --> 08:33.950
How can I thank you, Greg?

08:34.000 --> 08:37.950
You can meet me later, he says.

08:38.000 --> 08:44.950
After I go home and change out of my Porter's uniform.

08:45.000 --> 08:49.950
I'm sorry, Greg, says Cassie.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.950
I can't tonight.

08:53.000 --> 08:56.950
Maybe tomorrow night.

08:57.000 --> 08:59.950
Okay, says Greg.

09:00.000 --> 09:01.950
Tomorrow night.

09:02.000 --> 09:06.950
We can get something to eat first.

09:07.000 --> 09:10.950
Yes, okay, says Cassie.

09:11.000 --> 09:19.950
I have to go now, but meet me here tomorrow evening at six o'clock.

09:20.000 --> 09:23.950
Cassie gets up, ready to leave.

09:24.000 --> 09:28.950
Don't forget your key, says Greg.

09:29.000 --> 09:34.950
Oh, thanks, says Cassie.

09:35.000 --> 09:38.950
She takes it from him quickly.

09:39.000 --> 09:41.950
See you tomorrow.

09:42.000 --> 09:49.000
Greg is finishing his coffee when he sees his friend, Mike.

09:50.000 --> 09:54.950
You're in trouble, Greg, says Mike.

09:55.000 --> 09:59.950
Jake Russo's sketchbooks are not in his room.

10:00.000 --> 10:03.950
Room 724.

10:04.000 --> 10:11.950
And there are CCTV pictures of you coming from that room.

10:12.000 --> 10:19.950
Who is Jake Russo? asks Greg.

10:20.000 --> 10:24.950
Suddenly, he's not feeling very well.

10:25.000 --> 10:28.950
An artist, says Mike.

10:29.000 --> 10:33.950
His pictures sell for thousands of dollars.

10:34.000 --> 10:38.950
And his sketchbooks sell for thousands too.

10:39.000 --> 10:43.950
Do you have them? asks Mike.

10:44.000 --> 10:50.950
No, a girl has them, says Greg.

10:51.000 --> 10:54.950
What girl? asks Mike.

10:55.000 --> 10:59.950
A girl with green eyes, says Greg.

11:00.000 --> 11:06.000
And he tells Mike about Cassie and her stepfather.

11:07.000 --> 11:13.950
But it's not true, says Mike, when Greg finishes speaking.

11:14.000 --> 11:20.950
Jake Russo doesn't have a wife or a stepdaughter.

11:21.000 --> 11:26.950
You have to find that girl and get the sketchbooks, Greg.

11:27.000 --> 11:32.950
And you have to do it before the police find you.

11:33.000 --> 11:38.950
Greg walks home to his one room apartment.

11:39.000 --> 11:44.950
How am I going to find her? He thinks.

11:45.000 --> 11:54.950
She has Jake Russo's sketchbooks now, so she's not going to meet me again.

11:55.000 --> 12:01.000
Is she going to sell them for a lot of money?

12:02.000 --> 12:09.950
There is a police car in the street, next to Greg's apartment.

12:10.000 --> 12:14.950
Oh no, he thinks.

12:15.000 --> 12:17.950
They're waiting for me.

12:18.000 --> 12:23.950
I can't get into my apartment now.

12:24.000 --> 12:30.950
That night, Greg sleeps on a train in the subway.

12:31.000 --> 12:38.950
But early the next morning, Hey you, says a man.

12:39.000 --> 12:41.950
He's the subway cleaner.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.950
Get up.

12:44.000 --> 12:48.950
You can't sleep here all day.

12:49.000 --> 12:53.950
Sorry, says Greg.

12:54.000 --> 12:59.950
People are arriving to get their trains now.

13:00.000 --> 13:10.950
One of them stops and looks at a photograph in his newspaper, and then at Greg.

13:11.000 --> 13:15.950
It's him, thinks the man.

13:16.000 --> 13:21.950
It's the young man in the newspaper photograph.

13:22.000 --> 13:26.950
The police are looking for him.

13:27.000 --> 13:41.000
Suddenly, Greg sees the man looking at him, and he sees his picture on the front of the man's newspaper.

13:42.000 --> 13:48.950
I have to get out of here quickly. He thinks.

13:49.000 --> 13:54.950
The man with the newspaper finds a policeman.

13:55.000 --> 13:56.950
It's him.

13:57.000 --> 14:00.950
He tells the policeman.

14:01.000 --> 14:04.950
The hotel porter.

14:05.000 --> 14:07.950
Hey, you.

14:08.000 --> 14:11.950
The policeman calls to Greg.

14:12.000 --> 14:15.950
Greg runs.

14:16.000 --> 14:20.950
Stop! Calls the policeman.

14:21.000 --> 14:24.950
Greg doesn't stop.

14:25.000 --> 14:31.950
I have to get out of this uniform, thinks Greg.

14:32.000 --> 14:36.950
People know I'm the porter.

14:37.000 --> 14:43.950
Maybe Mike can give me something different to wear.

14:44.000 --> 14:50.950
When he gets to Mike's apartment, Mike opens the door.

14:51.000 --> 14:56.950
I need something to wear. Greg tells him.

14:57.000 --> 15:01.950
I can't go back to my apartment.

15:02.000 --> 15:10.950
I have pictures in the newspaper, and yes, I know, says Mike.

15:11.000 --> 15:13.950
It's okay.

15:14.000 --> 15:16.950
Come in.

15:17.000 --> 15:20.950
Way as the girl asks Mike.

15:21.000 --> 15:23.950
Do you know?

15:24.000 --> 15:27.950
No, says Greg.

15:28.000 --> 15:33.950
What can you remember about her? Says Mike.

15:34.000 --> 15:38.950
There must be something to help you find her.

15:39.000 --> 15:43.950
Yes, Greg says suddenly.

15:44.000 --> 15:46.950
Her key.

15:47.000 --> 15:52.950
A key to a room in the Dolphin Hotel.

15:53.000 --> 15:59.950
It's a small, cheap hotel near 42nd Street.

16:00.000 --> 16:03.950
She must be staying there.

16:04.000 --> 16:06.950
What's the time?

16:07.000 --> 16:12.950
Nearly nine o'clock, says Mike.

16:13.000 --> 16:17.950
Maybe she's there now, says Greg.

16:18.000 --> 16:21.950
I have to go.

16:22.000 --> 16:25.950
Thanks, Mike.

16:26.000 --> 16:32.950
Twenty minutes later, Greg is near the Dolphin Hotel.

16:33.000 --> 16:38.950
Am I too late? He thinks?

16:39.000 --> 16:45.950
Suddenly, Greg sees Cassie come out of the hotel.

16:46.000 --> 16:49.950
Cassie, he calls.

16:50.000 --> 16:51.950
Wait.

16:52.000 --> 16:56.950
I have to talk to you.

16:57.000 --> 17:02.950
Cassie sees him, but she doesn't stop.

17:03.000 --> 17:07.950
There is a car waiting for her.

17:08.000 --> 17:15.950
She says something to the driver and gets into it quickly.

17:16.000 --> 17:20.950
Oh, no, says Greg.

17:21.000 --> 17:25.950
Here, 83.

17:26.000 --> 17:29.950
Says an old man in the street.

17:30.000 --> 17:33.950
Greg looks at him.

17:34.000 --> 17:35.950
What?

17:36.000 --> 17:55.950
The girl is going to peer 83 West 42nd Street for the circle line boat. Says the old man.

17:56.000 --> 17:58.950
Greg smiles.

17:59.000 --> 18:02.950
Thanks, he says.

18:03.000 --> 18:06.950
And he begins to run.

18:07.000 --> 18:14.950
Greg runs all the way to peer 83.

18:15.000 --> 18:23.950
People are getting on to the boat, and he gets a ticket.

18:24.000 --> 18:29.950
On the boat, Greg looks for Cassie.

18:30.000 --> 18:35.950
But a woman with a newspaper is looking at him.

18:36.000 --> 18:42.950
It's the young man in the picture. She tells the man with her.

18:43.000 --> 18:47.950
Call the police, Eddie.

18:48.000 --> 18:54.950
The man gets his phone and calls the police.

18:55.000 --> 19:00.950
Some time later, Greg sees Cassie.

19:01.000 --> 19:04.950
She is talking to a man.

19:05.000 --> 19:12.950
But Greg does not see two policemen get on the boat.

19:13.000 --> 19:16.950
They quickly find Greg.

19:17.000 --> 19:25.950
Where are Jake Russo's sketchbooks? The first policeman asks him.

19:26.000 --> 19:31.950
I don't have them, says Greg.

19:32.000 --> 19:34.950
You don't want me.

19:35.000 --> 19:37.950
You want her.

19:38.000 --> 19:42.950
She has the sketchbooks.

19:43.000 --> 19:51.950
Hey, look. He's right. Says the second policeman.

19:52.000 --> 19:58.950
The two policemen move quickly to Cassie and the man.

19:59.000 --> 20:04.950
I don't understand, says Cassie.

20:05.000 --> 20:06.950
How?

20:07.000 --> 20:14.950
The two of you are coming with us, says one of the policemen.

20:15.000 --> 20:18.950
You're in trouble.

20:19.000 --> 20:27.950
Later, Greg and a policeman take the sketchbooks back to the hotel.

20:28.000 --> 20:34.950
Jake Russo is very happy to see them again.

20:35.000 --> 20:43.950
I'm sorry, Mr. Russo, says Greg, and tells him everything.

20:44.000 --> 20:50.950
It's okay, says the artist, smiling.

20:51.000 --> 20:59.000
But stay away from girls with beautiful green eyes.
